    "\$V = 2\\pi \\int_{0}^{1} x \\cdot x^{3} \\, dx = 2\\pi \\int_{0}^{1} x^{4} \\, dx\$. An antiderivative is \$F(x) = \\dfrac{x^{5}}{5}\$, so \$V = 2\\pi \\left[F(1)-F(0)\\right] = 2\\pi \\left[\\dfrac{1}{5} - 0\\right] = \\dfrac{2\\pi}{5}\$.",
    "\$V = 2\\pi \\int_{0}^{3} x \\cdot x \\, dx = 2\\pi \\int_{0}^{3} x^{2} \\, dx\$. An antiderivative is \$F(x) = \\dfrac{x^{3}}{3}\$, so \$V = 2\\pi \\left[F(3)-F(0)\\right] = 2\\pi \\left[9 - 0\\right] = 18\\pi\$.",
    "\$V = 2\\pi \\int_{0}^{4} x \\cdot \\sqrt{x} \\, dx = 2\\pi \\int_{0}^{4} x^{3/2} \\, dx\$. An antiderivative is \$F(x) = \\dfrac{2}{5}x^{5/2}\$, so \$V = 2\\pi \\left[F(4)-F(0)\\right] = 2\\pi \\left[\\dfrac{2}{5}(32) - 0\\right] = 2\\pi \\cdot \\dfrac{64}{5} = \\dfrac{128\\pi}{5}\$.",
    "\$V = \\pi \\int_{0}^{1} [x^{2}]^2 \\, dx = \\pi \\int_{0}^{1} x^{4} \\, dx\$. An antiderivative of the integrand is \$F(x) = \\frac{x^{5}}{5}\$, so \$V = \\pi \\left[F(1) - F(0)\\right] = \\pi \\left[\\frac{1^{5}}{5} - \\left(\\frac{0^{5}}{5}\\right)\\right] = \\frac{\\pi}{5}\$.",
    "\$V = \\pi \\int_{0}^{3} [2]^2 \\, dx = \\pi \\int_{0}^{3} 4 \\, dx\$. An antiderivative of the integrand is \$F(x) = 4 x\$, so \$V = \\pi \\left[F(3) - F(0)\\right] = \\pi \\left[4 \\cdot 3 - \\left(4 \\cdot 0\\right)\\right] = 12 \\pi\$.",
    "\$V = \\pi \\int_{0}^{4} [\\sqrt{x}]^2 \\, dx = \\pi \\int_{0}^{4} x \\, dx\$. An antiderivative of the integrand is \$F(x) = \\frac{x^{2}}{2}\$, so \$V = \\pi \\left[F(4) - F(0)\\right] = \\pi \\left[\\frac{4^{2}}{2} - \\left(\\frac{0^{2}}{2}\\right)\\right] = 8 \\pi\$.",
    "\$V = \\pi \\int_{0}^{4} [x]^2 \\, dx = \\pi \\int_{0}^{4} x^{2} \\, dx\$. An antiderivative of the integrand is \$F(x) = \\frac{x^{3}}{3}\$, so \$V = \\pi \\left[F(4) - F(0)\\right] = \\pi \\left[\\frac{4^{3}}{3} - \\left(\\frac{0^{3}}{3}\\right)\\right] = \\frac{64 \\pi}{3}\$.",
    "\$V=\\pi\\int_{0}^{1} x^2\\,dx = \\pi\\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3}\\right]_{0}^{1} = \\pi\\cdot\\frac{1}{3}\$.",
    "\$V=\\pi\\int_{0}^{2} x^2\\,dx = \\pi\\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3}\\right]_{0}^{2} = \\pi\\cdot\\frac{8}{3}\$.",
    "\$V=\\pi\\int_{0}^{3} x^2\\,dx = \\pi\\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3}\\right]_{0}^{3} = \\pi\\cdot9\$.",
