    "\$\\dfrac{dx}{dt} = -\\sin(t)\$ and \$\\dfrac{dy}{dt} = \\cos(t)\$. So \$\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = \\dfrac{\\cos(t)}{-\\sin(t)} = -\\cot(t)\$.",
