    "\$\\dfrac{dx}{dt} = 2t\$ and \$\\dfrac{dy}{dt} = 2t+1\$. So \$\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = \\dfrac{dy/dt}{dx/dt} = \\dfrac{2t+1}{2t}\$.",
    "\$\\dfrac{dx}{dt} = 3t^{2}\$ and \$\\dfrac{dy}{dt} = 2t\$, so \$\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = \\dfrac{2t}{3t^{2}} = \\dfrac{2}{3t}\$.",
    "\$\\dfrac{dx}{dt}=2t\$, \$\\dfrac{dy}{dt}=3t^2\$, so \$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{3t^2}{2t}=\\dfrac{3t}{2}\$. At \$t=1\$: \$\\dfrac{3(1)}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}\$.",
    "\$\\dfrac{dx}{dt}=2t\$, \$\\dfrac{dy}{dt}=3t^2\$, so \$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{3t^2}{2t}=\\dfrac{3t}{2}\$. At \$t=2\$: \$\\dfrac{3(2)}{2}=3\$.",
    "\$\\dfrac{dx}{dt}=2t\$, \$\\dfrac{dy}{dt}=3t^2\$, so \$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{3t^2}{2t}=\\dfrac{3t}{2}\$. At \$t=3\$: \$\\dfrac{3(3)}{2}=\\frac{9}{2}\$.",
    "\$\\dfrac{dx}{dt}=2t\$, \$\\dfrac{dy}{dt}=3t^2\$, so \$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{3t^2}{2t}=\\dfrac{3t}{2}\$. At \$t=4\$: \$\\dfrac{3(4)}{2}=6\$.",
    "\$\\dfrac{dx}{dt}=2t\$, \$\\dfrac{dy}{dt}=3t^2\$, so \$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{3t^2}{2t}=\\dfrac{3t}{2}\$. At \$t=5\$: \$\\dfrac{3(5)}{2}=\\frac{15}{2}\$.",
