    "\$f'(x) = 2 \\left(x - 2\\right)\$. Solving \$f'(x) > 0\$ shows \$f'(x)\$ is positive for \$x \\in \\left(2, \\infty\\right)\$, so \$f\$ is increasing on \$\\left(2, \\infty\\right)\$.",
    "\$f'(x) = 2 e^{2x}\$ by the chain rule. Differentiating again, \$f''(x) = 2 \\cdot 2 e^{2x} = 4 e^{2x}\$.",
