    "\$f'(x) = 2x - 4 = 0\$ at \$x=2\$, an interior critical point. Checking \$f\$ at the critical point and both endpoints: \$f(0)=3\$, \$f(2) = 4-8+3=-1\$, \$f(5) = 25-20+3=8\$. The smallest of these is \$f(2) = -1\$, so the absolute minimum on \$[0,5]\$ is \$-1\$.",
    "\$f'(x) = 2x - 4\$. Setting \$f'(c) = 0\$: \$2c - 4 = 0 \\Rightarrow c = 2\$, which indeed lies in \$(1,3)\$, confirming Rolle's Theorem.",
    "\$f'(x) = 3 \\left(x - 1\\right) \\left(x + 1\\right)\$. Solving \$f'(x) < 0\$ shows \$f'(x)\$ is negative for \$x \\in \\left(-1, 1\\right)\$, so \$f\$ is decreasing on \$\\left(-1, 1\\right)\$.",
    "\$f'(x) = 3 x^{2} - 12\$. Setting \$f'(x) = 0\$: \$3 x^{2} - 12 = 0\$, which gives \$x = -2, 2\$.",
