    "Since \$f^{-1}(x) = \\sqrt{x}\$ for \$x \\geq 0\$, \$f^{-1}(9) = \\sqrt{9} = 3\$. (Check: \$f(3) = 3^{2} = 9\$, confirming the inverse.)",
    "Since \$x+2 \\geq x^{2}\$ on \$[-1,2]\$, Area \$= \\int_{-1}^{2} [(x+2)-x^{2}]\\,dx\$. An antiderivative is \$F(x)=\\dfrac{x^{2}}{2}+2x-\\dfrac{x^{3}}{3}\$, giving \$F(2)-F(-1) = \\dfrac{16}{3} - \\left(-\\dfrac{7}{6}\\right) = \\dfrac{9}{2}\$.",
    "Since the numerator and denominator have the same degree, the horizontal asymptote is the ratio of leading coefficients: \$y = \\dfrac{2}{1} = 2\$, confirmed by \$\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} \\dfrac{2x^{2}+1}{x^{2}-4} = 2\$.",
